          "_label": "Details (Official List Description)"
        }
      ],
      "content": "NORTHCHURCH            \tWHARF LANE SP 90 NE \t\t\t\t\t(North side)                                        \t\tDudswell                                          3/241                                   \tArne Cottage 30.11.66                                \t(formerly listed as Arne Dudswell) -                                        \tII House. Late C16 N range, incorporating late medieval bay at E. Inserted floor and chimney of early C17, and taller early C18 S wing. Timber frame on brick sill, red brick infill and walls to S wing, painted brick infill on N front. Steep old red tile roofs. An L-shaped house facing N, of 1½ storeys with 2 storeys and attic S wing. N front has regular square panels of timber framing, 2 gabled dormers, 2 casement windows and a boarded door into W bay. Large internal chimney in E bay serving middle bay. 2 bays remain of original house, both once open to the roof. Floor beams and joists in both bays appear of same date. E bay the hall, W bay probably parlour and store room. House probably extended further to E but removed when rear S wing built leaving cross passage preserved as a store room. (RCHM Typescript). Listing NGR: SP9656909798"
    }
  ],
